## Harness Engineering (Codex)

- Keep the project's existing instructions and task scope authoritative.
- Delivery: {{DELIVERY}}. Use exactly one skill delivery route; do not enable the same harness plugin alongside project skills.
- {{RESOURCE_LAYOUT}}
- Before a workflow, read its SKILL.md and harness-delta.md, use the relevant platform reference under `{{RUNTIME_ROOT}}/references/platforms/` for host-specific differences. Do not assume Claude-specific tools are available.
- Track requirements in root `features.json`. Use `docs/harness-progress.json`, falling back to legacy `docs/claude-progress.json` without deleting it.
- Plan → test-first implementation → verification → archive; preserve scope and existing authorization. Map tools to actual available capabilities and disclose unavailable automation.
- Configuration is `.harness/config.json`. Default: no auto-commit, Issue sync, push, deploy or global settings changes.
- Explicit checks: `python3 {{RUNTIME_ROOT}}/scripts/harness_runtime.py verify --project .` after configuring verification_commands as argv arrays.
- Hooks are optional and require native trust review. Project skill installation alone does not activate hooks or provide security enforcement.
<!-- harness:end -->
